{
  "id": "training-modules-2025",
  "title": "ISET Orientation Training Modules (2025-2026)",
  "source": { "deckId": "TRAINING MODULES - September 2025" },
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "program-overview-agreement",
      "title": "Program overview & agreement",
      "isOptional": false,
      "tags": ["overview", "agreement", "funding", "eligibility"],
      "roles": ["Case Manager", "PTMA Lead", "Admin"],
      "estimatedMinutes": 6,
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "s1-what-this-orientation-covers",
          "title": "What this orientation covers",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 1 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Orientation to the ISET program and NWAC's contribution agreement for case managers, PTMA leads, and administrators - covering mandate, EI/CRF funding streams, eligibility, documentation, case management cadence, and compliance expectations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-contribution-agreement-funding",
          "title": "Contribution agreement & funding",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 3 },
          "tags": ["funding", "ei", "crf"],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "NWAC holds a ten-year contribution agreement with ESDC (2019-2029) valued at about $33M.",
                "Funding flows through two streams each year: Employment Insurance (EI) for clients who qualify under EI rules, and the Consolidated Revenue Fund (CRF) for costs that are not EI-eligible.",
                "CRF dollars can be shifted to cover EI-eligible costs, but EI dollars cannot be moved into CRF uses.",
                "The ISET mandate is to increase Indigenous participation in the labour market through training and education and to close employment and earnings gaps."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s4-who-delivers-iset",
          "title": "Who delivers ISET",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 4 },
          "tags": ["delivery"],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "NWAC is one of two national ISET holders. Founded in 1974, NWAC serves First Nations, Inuit, and Metis women in all their diversities, on- and off-reserve, status and non-status.",
                "Across Canada there are more than 115 regional ISET holders. NWAC may sign sub-agreements with PTMAs (13 grassroots organizations; 10 active as of Oct 2024) to deliver the program regionally.",
                "PTMAs and regional ISET managers handle service delivery, case management, employer and education partnerships, community outreach, and data compliance."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s7-eligibility-identity-proof",
          "title": "Eligibility & identity proof",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 7 },
          "tags": ["eligibility", "identity"],
          "roles": ["Case Manager"],
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Eligibility: Canadian citizen; Indigenous women in all their diversities (status/non-status First Nations, Metis, Inuit; urban, rural, remote); unemployed, under-employed, or at risk; not an active NWAC/PTMA staff member or board member.",
                "Identity proof: Status/Treaty/Nation card plus a signed Indigenous self-declaration. If no card, provide two reference letters from Indigenous leadership and/or ISC evidence of identity/heritage.",
                "Self-declaration alone is not enough. Two pieces of ID are required; when available, one must be the Status/Treaty card."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "intake-consent-verification",
      "title": "Intake, consent & eligibility verification",
      "isOptional": true,
      "tags": ["intake", "consent", "ei", "arms"],
      "roles": ["Case Manager"],
      "estimatedMinutes": 6,
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "s27-application-intake-arms-setup",
          "title": "Application intake & ARMS setup",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 27 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Intake sources include the web form, walk-ins, job fairs/community events, and referrals.",
                "Within 5 business days acknowledge receipt, request missing items, and set a deadline. Close the file after three attempts with no response; the client must then re-apply.",
                "Create and activate the client in ARMS as soon as the application arrives. Upload all documents and record every interaction."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s39-ei-crf-routing-consent",
          "title": "EI/CRF routing & client consent",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 39 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Obtain the signed Client Consent for EI Verification before any check. Submit the EI Verification Request with the consent to the Associate/Senior Director; expect an LMDA response in about 2-3 business days.",
                "Documents to review and sign: Client Funding Agreement (after approval), Authorization for Release of ISET Client Information, Client Acknowledgement of Funding Source, Consent for Images/Audio, and Conflict of Interest Declaration.",
                "CRA reminder: A T4A is issued for all ISET funding and clients must report it. Tax exemption decisions are made by CRA, not by case managers."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s43-processing-timelines-compliance",
          "title": "Processing timelines & file compliance",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 43 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Process complete applications within roughly three weeks (depending on volume) after all documents are received. Status remains \"pending\" until NWAC approves and the funding agreement is signed.",
                "Files must be audit-ready: accurate, current, and consistent data and uploads in ARMS, compliant with ESDC/NWAC privacy and data standards.",
                "Close out intakes promptly if they are ineligible or incomplete, and record the determination."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "financial-assessment-supports",
      "title": "Financial assessment & supports",
      "isOptional": true,
      "tags": ["financial", "living-allowance", "tuition"],
      "roles": ["Case Manager", "PTMA Lead"],
      "estimatedMinutes": 7,
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "s54-financial-overview-verification",
          "title": "Financial overview & verification",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 54 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The client must complete the Financial Overview, disclose all household income and funding sources, and provide proof before any recommendation.",
                "Income verification may include three recent paystubs (client/partner), child tax statement, proof of alimony/child support, social assistance letters, ROE or tax assessments, and bank statements if needed.",
                "Band/Treaty letters: a current denial letter on official letterhead (matching the program and term) is required if Band funding is unavailable. A funding letter may make the client ineligible for a living allowance to avoid double-dipping."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s58-expenses-living-allowance",
          "title": "Expenses & living allowance rules",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 58 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Verify expenses when a living allowance is requested (childcare, rent/mortgage, basic utilities, transportation).",
                "Living allowance: needs-based subsidy during training only; not retroactive; not intended to cover all expenses or debts; not payable while an EI claim is active; monthly attendance reports are required.",
                "Eligible coverage: rent/mortgage, basic utilities, groceries, transit, and incremental childcare tied to training. Ineligible: debt payments, car payments/insurance, entertainment, subscriptions, and most non-training costs."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s70-program-costs-documentation",
          "title": "Program costs & documentation",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 70 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Eligible costs include tuition and fees at accredited institutions, essential skills/upgrading, diplomas/certificates, degrees, job search or self-employment services, exam/licence fees, required books/materials, and specialized equipment with proof and a quote.",
                "The Letter of Acceptance and Statement of Fees must be current, on official letterhead or portal, and match the program; provide annual confirmation for multi-year programs.",
                "Tuition is normally paid directly to the provider. Reimbursements require prior approval and original paid receipts. Specialized equipment over $650 needs NWAC pre-approval; provide receipts within two weeks if funds are advanced."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "interventions-planning",
      "title": "Interventions & planning",
      "isOptional": true,
      "tags": ["interventions", "planning", "assessment"],
      "roles": ["Case Manager"],
      "estimatedMinutes": 7,
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "s11-intervention-design-research",
          "title": "Intervention design & research",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 11 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An intervention is an Individualized Action Plan activity with a defined timeframe to improve employability.",
                "Case manager research: confirm the career or training choice is realistic; explain physical and mental demands; check labour market demand, wages, and progression (including tech/AI/Red Seal fields); ensure credentials lead to viable employment; aim to close earnings gaps.",
                "Multiple interventions are allowed when each aligns with the needs assessment and improves employment potential."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s12-employability-dimensions",
          "title": "Employability dimensions & assessment",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 12 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Career decision: assess the client's ability to choose and research options; use diagnostics if needed.",
                "Skills enhancement: place clients in training or education to obtain required competencies and credentials (essential skills, academic upgrading, occupational training).",
                "Work experience: options include student employment, wage subsidy, job creation partnerships, or a self-employment pathway.",
                "Resume: required. Use it to verify history, identify transferable skills, guide planning, and explore alternatives."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s13-case-manager-assessment",
          "title": "Case manager assessment & recommendation",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 13 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Assess the application against eligibility, documentation, research, and employability dimensions; keep data consistent across documents and ARMS.",
                "Recommendations must include justification (goals, labour market fit, research, prior interventions). You may recommend alternate interventions or decline funding if not aligned.",
                "Send all recommendations to NWAC for approval. NWAC will approve, deny, or request changes, and the case manager communicates the decision to the client."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "funding-streams-options",
      "title": "Funding streams & program options",
      "isOptional": true,
      "tags": ["funding", "streams", "programs"],
      "roles": ["Case Manager", "PTMA Lead"],
      "estimatedMinutes": 6,
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "s14-itp",
          "title": "Individual Training Purchase (ITP)",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 14 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Covers tuition and fees, related program costs, and living expenses (if eligible) for approved training programs.",
                "Client must supply current program details and costs; verify the program leads to employment in the chosen field.",
                "Use program databases and labour market research to support the recommendation."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s18-tws",
          "title": "Targeted Wage Subsidy (TWS)",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 18 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Encourages employers to hire and train clients with on-the-job experience; supports up to 8 hours per day. Non-profits are eligible for maximum subsidy; private sector is typically about 50% of wages plus MERCs/vacation.",
                "Employer must provide: outline of duties, a letter of offer after the subsidy ends, and an employment plan with orientation and job description.",
                "Student employment variant helps full-time students gain work experience."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s20-jcp-seb-group-training",
          "title": "JCP, SEB, group training",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 20 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Job Creation Partnership (JCP): temporary jobs that benefit the client and the community; public or non-profit only (no private sector); intended to improve long-term employment prospects.",
                "Self-Employment Benefits (SEB): financial assistance plus business training/support for start-up, business plan development, and marketing/accounting advice; incubator partnerships are eligible.",
                "Group training/special projects: regional projects that combine certification, life skills, pre-employment, or work experience; require a capable sponsor with management capacity and liability coverage; can run up to 52 weeks."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "case-management-reporting-compliance",
      "title": "Case management, reporting & compliance",
      "isOptional": true,
      "tags": ["case-management", "reporting", "compliance", "arms"],
      "roles": ["Case Manager", "PTMA Lead", "Admin"],
      "estimatedMinutes": 6,
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "s24-case-management-cadence",
          "title": "Case management cadence",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 24 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Provide case management for the full intervention: monthly check-ins (or as needed) using trauma-informed, culturally safe engagement.",
                "Track attendance and milestones; document in ARMS; celebrate progress; adapt plans to address barriers; refer to community supports (mental health, housing, safety).",
                "Follow up for 12 weeks after the intervention ends and close files with clear outcomes."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s33-planning-outreach-partnerships",
          "title": "Planning, outreach & partnerships",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 33 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Regional workplan: define priorities and goals, timelines, employer and education partnerships, outreach and events, budgeting/forecasting, and risk mitigation.",
                "Outreach: respect cultural protocols; engage Elders and knowledge keepers; align messaging to community values; maintain relationships beyond promotion.",
                "Partnerships: identify aligned employers/providers; explain ISET benefits; co-host pipelines or fairs; keep partners engaged and culturally informed."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s86-reporting-authorization",
          "title": "Reporting & authorization",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 86 },
          "requiresAcknowledgement": true,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reporting: maintain the ISET advance and active client spreadsheet; submit at least every 90 days; track costs, start/end dates, and outcomes. Track Minimum Service Level interactions for non-funded services.",
                "Authorization to Quit / Section 25: use only in active case management and close to start; it allows EI Part I claims while training. Use the ATQ form and Training Referral per delegation rules.",
                "ARMS compliance: enter all applications (funded and unfunded); upload documents and notes. NWAC conducts audits and escalates non-compliance."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s93-contacts",
          "title": "Contacts",
          "source": { "slideNumber": 93 },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "contacts",
              "items": [
                { "name": "National ISET Associate Director", "email": "mcoppola@nwac.ca", "phone": "343-961-7909" },
                { "name": "Senior Director, Economic Development", "email": "sstacey@nwac.ca", "phone": "343-961-3431" },
                { "name": "Regional ISET Manager (QC)", "email": "emarion@nwac.ca", "phone": "613-404-5095" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
